    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d684">

                <pb facs="0807" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg711"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Storer.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>You will express to the minister of state the President’s appreciation of the
                    considerate decision of the council of ministers to pay inscriptions of
                    thirty-four without waiting negotiation of new convention. It would be agreeable
                    to us to have place and manner of payment as heretofore.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
